    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="30.8">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 30.8</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.8" corresp="#wit-g-a">Gyf seo lad forðcume, beo he þæs weres wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30.8" corresp="#wit-a">Gif seo lad forðcyme, beo he þæs weres wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30.8" corresp="#wit-q">Si purgatio perficiatur, sit wérę suę dignus.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="30.8" corresp="#wit-b">Gyf seo lád [forðcume, beo he þæs weres wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">Gyf seo lad forðcume, beo he þæs weres wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">If he succeeds in clearing himself, he shall be entitled to the wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">If the exoneration is successful, he will be entitled to the wergild.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And if the exculpation succeeds, he is to be entitled to the wergild.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn diese Reinigung zu Stande kommt, so sei er zu jenem Wergeld [seines Untergebenen] berechtigt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If the clearing succeeds, let him be entitled to that wergild [of his dependant].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="335"><ref target="clause:IAtr_1-9">I Atr 1.9</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. I Atr. 1, 9</note>
        <note type="editorial">B skips a line here. Liebermann compares I Atr 1.9.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">forðcume . . . wyrðe: omitted B</note>
      </div>
